[center]Are you struggling to [b]keep track of faction presence and growth[/b]?
Do you want to know [b]which systems are claimed and by who[/b] before you even take the trip there?
Do you want to [b]paint the map[/b] with your conquests?
Do you just want to [b]see all that border gore[/b] factions in your mod list produce?
Do you want to [b][url=https://www.reddit.com/r/starsector/comments/1wl36nq/finally_bad_apple_thanks_kmu/]play Bad Apple[/url][/b]?[/center]

[b][color=#ffff00]Sector Map Layers[/color][/b] is an overlay for the [color=#00ffff]map screen [b](Tab, Q)[/b][/color], the [color=#00ffff]intel screen [/color][b][color=#00ffff](E, 1)[/color][/b], the [color=#00ffff]minimap[/color] in the bottom right corner of the screen (replaces the vanilla [color=#00ffff]radar[/color]) if you have [b][color=#ffff00]Random Assortment of Things[/color][/b] installed.

Everything is calculated and drawn off of game data, and it gets updated as the state of the sector changes. Map layers don't alter any of the data being used to draw it, making [color=#00ff00]map layers [b]read-only[/b] by design[/color].

Full mod information is [url=https://fractalsoftworks.com/forum/index.php?topic=36029.0]available on [b]Fractal Softworks[/b] forum[/url].

[b][size=4]Installation instructions[/size][/b]

Recommended: [url=https://trilink.wispborne.com/open.html?mod=%7B%22url%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FKlark-Morrigan%2FStarsector-Mod-KMU%2Freleases%2Flatest%2Fdownload%2Fkmu.version%22%2C%22id%22%3A%22kmu%22%7D&dep=%7B%22url%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2FLazyWizard%2Flazylib%2Fmaster%2Fmod%2Flazylib.version%22%2C%22id%22%3A%22lw_lazylib%22%7D&dep=%7B%22url%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2FLukas22041%2FLunaLib%2Fmain%2FLunaLib.version%22%2C%22id%22%3A%22lunalib%22%7D&dep=%7B%22url%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FKlark-Morrigan%2FStarsector-Mod-KMLib%2Freleases%2Flatest%2Fdownload%2Fkmlib.version%22%2C%22id%22%3A%22kmlib%22%7D]instal with [b]TriOS[/b][/url] (latest versions of the mod and its dependencies)

Manual:

[list]
[*]Download [b][url=https://fractalsoftworks.com/forum/index.php?topic=5444.0]LazyLib[/url][/b], [b][url=https://fractalsoftworks.com/forum/index.php?topic=25658.0]LunaLib[/url][/b], [b]KMLib[/b], [b]KMU[/b]. (Download mirrors always point to latest versions.)[/*]
[*]Unzip each mod into your [b]starsector/mods[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Enable each mod in the game launcher.[/*]
[/list]

It's [b][color=#00ff00]safe[/color] to install mid-run[/b],
and there's a short [b][color=#00ff00]uninstall procedure[/color][/b] you will need to follow if you decide to keep your save after uninstalling the mod.

[b][color=#ffff00]KMU[/color][/b] comes with [b][color=#ffff00]Sector Map Layers[/color][/b] feature [color=#00ff00]turned on by default[/color]. After loading a save or starting a new game, when you open the [b][color=#00ffff]map screen[/color][/b] or the [b][color=#00ffff]intel screen[/color][/b], you'll see a new [b][color=#00ffff]Map layers[/color][/b] button among map filter buttons. Clicking that button or pressing [b][color=#00ffff](M)[/color][/b] enables the map layer overlay and its sidebar.

The main control interface of map layers is the [color=#00ffff]collapsible [b]sidebar[/b][/color] that lists all available layers and related knobs and toggles.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

The map overlay is broadly compatible because the game and other mods reuse the map widget.
The UI component must be made aware of any modded UI it overlaps to avoid obstruction.
Mods with explicit compatibility:

[list]
[*][color=#ffff00][size=3][b]Fast Rendering[/b][/size][/color][/*]
[*][color=#ffff00][size=3][b]Console Commands[/b][/size][/color][/*]
[*][color=#ffff00][size=3][b]Nexerelin[/b][/size][/color][/*]
[*][size=3][b][color=#ffff00]Random Assortment of Things[/color][/b][/size][/*]
[/list]
